  <section id="privacy">
    <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

    <h3>What this app does</h3>
    <p>Teleport is a developer utility that lets you simulate ("mock") a device's GPS location for the purpose of testing location-based app features. It does this using Android's built-in test location provider APIs.</p>

    <h3>Information we access</h3>
    <div class="card">
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Location data</strong> — used only to display your current position on the in-app map and to let you set/save mock locations. This data stays on your device.</li>
        <li><strong>Saved locations</strong> — any places you save (name + coordinates) are stored locally on your device.</li>
        <li><strong>Search queries</strong> — if you use the search bar, your query is sent to Google's Places/Maps API to return location suggestions. This is subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>What we do NOT do</h3>
    <div class="card">
      <ul>
        <li>We do not collect, transmit, or store your location data on any external server.</li>
        <li>We do not sell or share your data with third parties.</li>
        <li>We do not track your real-world movements or usage history outside your device.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>Permissions</h3>
    <p>The app requests location, notification (for the background service indicator), and storage/file-picker access (for GPX route import). Each is used solely for the feature described and nothing else.</p>

    <h3>Children's privacy</h3>
    <p>Teleport is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect data from children under 13 (or the relevant age in your jurisdiction).</p>

    <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
    <p>If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date above will be revised. Continued use of the app after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms">
    <h2>Terms of Service</h2>

    <div class="warn">
      <strong>Intended use:</strong> Teleport is provided as a development and testing tool for simulating GPS location during app/software development, QA testing, and debugging location-based features. It is not intended to help you misrepresent your location to third-party services, games, or platforms in violation of their own terms of service.
    </div>

    <h3>Acceptable use</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>You may use Teleport on devices you own or have explicit permission to test on.</li>
      <li>You are solely responsible for complying with the terms of service of any other app or platform you use alongside Teleport. Using mock location to circumvent another service's location checks may violate that service's terms and could result in penalties (such as account suspension) imposed by that service — not by us.</li>
      <li>You may not use this app for any unlawful purpose, including but not limited to fraud, stalking, harassment, or evading legal or safety obligations tied to location reporting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>No warranty</h3>
    <p>Teleport is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We do not guarantee that mock locations will be accepted by every app or service, or that the app will be free of bugs.</p>

    <h3>Limitation of liability</h3>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the developer is not liable for any damages, losses, account actions, or consequences arising from your use or misuse of this app, including actions taken against you by third-party services as a result of location spoofing.</p>

    <h3>Changes</h3>
    <p>We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the app after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.</p>
  </section>

